<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan's grain import values rise in September.</title>
<headline>Taiwan's grain import values rise in September.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The value of Taiwan's grain and oilseed imports in September was US$257.6 million, up 30.6 percent from US$197.3 million in September 1995, the Finance Ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>Taiwan traders attributed the rise in grain import values to the high international prices during September.</p>
<p>September tonnages were not available.</p>
<p>The following is a table of major grain import figures in millions of U.S. dollars:</p>
<p>		   September 1996    September 1995</p>
<p> Wheat		   20.7	     18.8</p>
<p> Corn		   101.4	     80.6</p>
<p> Soybeans		55.1	     47.9</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
